@PIXEL_TITLE@  -  version @PROJECT_VERSION@
==================================================

A pixel-art roguelike shooter. Fight through three sectors of drifting rocks and flying saucers,
pick an upgrade after every wave, beat a boss at the end of each sector - with one ship. Spend
the scrap from your runs in the hangar on new ships and upgrades.

Run @PIXEL_FILE_NAME@.exe. No installation needed; keep the "shaders" and "assets" folders next
to the .exe.


CONTROLS
--------
                   Keyboard                  Gamepad (Xbox / PlayStation / Switch)
  Rotate           A / D  or  Left / Right   left stick or d-pad
  Thrust           W  or  Up                 left stick up, right trigger or d-pad up
  Fire (hold)      Space                     A / Cross (bottom button) or right shoulder
  Hyperspace       Shift                     Y / Triangle (top button)
  Pause / menu     Esc  or  P                Start / Options / +
  Fullscreen       F11  or  Alt+Enter
  Mute             M                         View / Share / -

Menus, the upgrade picker and the hangar: Up / Down / Left / Right to choose, Enter / Space
(or A) to confirm, Esc (or B) to go back. The hangar is in the title screen menu (Esc).


A RUN
-----
- 3 sectors x 4 waves, and a boss at the end of each sector. One ship: when it's destroyed, the
  run is over. Beat the third boss to win.
- After each wave choose one of three upgrades. They stack:
    Spread shot, Piercing rounds, Rapid fire, Shield (absorbs a hit, recharges every wave),
    Thruster, Hyper blast (hyperspace damages what's near), and from the hangar: Homing
    missiles, Rear gun, Long range, Scrap magnet.
- Rocks: plain, explosive (they blow up everything near them - you too), metal (several hits)
  and green splitters (three fast pieces). Saucers get tougher in deeper sectors.
- Bosses: The Monolith, The Mothership and The Bastion.
- Collect the scrap that destroyed things drop. At the end of a run you earn that scrap plus a
  bonus for every wave, boss and 250 points.


HANGAR
------
Ships: Striker (free), Bulwark (starts with a shield), Wasp (fast, rapid fire), Lancer (piercing
long shots). Upgrades bought here join the pool the run's offers are drawn from.


OPTIONS AND SAVED FILES
-----------------------
Options (pause menu or title screen menu): master volume, effects volume, fullscreen, vsync,
screen shake, particles, and the controls. Settings, the high scores, the hangar progress and
the log file are kept in your user folder:
  Windows:  %APPDATA%\Ridejock\@PIXEL_FILE_NAME@\
            (settings.txt, highscores.txt, meta.txt, logs\@PIXEL_FILE_NAME@.log)
Delete meta.txt to start the hangar over, highscores.txt to reset the table.

Needs Windows 10 or 11 and a graphics driver with Direct3D 12 or Vulkan support.


CREDITS
-------
Game, code, sound design and art: Ervin Ashley.
Every sound is synthesized by the game while it starts; there are no recordings.

Made with the Emerald engine (https://github.com/Ridejock/Emerald) on top of SDL3
(https://libsdl.org). Also uses spdlog, {fmt}, stb, dr_mp3 and nlohmann/json.

